d_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.26043560359395235,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.013484619669877906,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":66.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01952,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":13.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"MFA Financial, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a real estate investment trust in the United States. It operates through two segments: Mortgage-Related Assets and Lima One. The Mortgage-Related Assets segment primarily invests in and manages a diversified portfolio of residential whole loans, including nonqualified mortgage loans, business purpose loans such as single-family rental loans, single-family and multifamily transitional loans, legacy re-performing and non-performing loans, and agency-eligible investor loans. This segment also invests in residential mortgage-backed securities, including agency MBS, non-agency MBS, and credit risk transfer securities. The Lima One segment includes a stand-alone mortgage origination and servicing business; and originates and services business purpose loans for real estate investors, and related mortgage banking activities. The company offers residential whole loans, including purchased credit deteriorated and non-performing loans; and mortgage servicing rights-related assets. The company's investment activities through a combination of securitization transactions, term loan warehouse financing and repurchase agreement financing. The company qualifies as a real estate investment trust for federal income tax purposes. It generally would not be subject to federal corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. MFA Financial, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Craig L. Knutson | CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 307 people. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MFA Financial, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $628M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 26.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 143% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 65% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MFA Financial Inc (MFA) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Book Value Slides on Rate Volatility ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/mfa-financial-inc-mfa-q3-230545233.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794006345.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MFA Financial (NYSE:MFA) Reaches New 12-Month Low After Earnings Miss","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/mfa-financial-nysemfa-reaches-new-12-month-low-after-earnings-miss.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793911965.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MFA Financial (MFA) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/mfa-financial-mfa-q3-2026-141609704.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793888169.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MFA Financial Reports $111.7M Net Loss in Q3 2026 Amid Fair Value Challenge